  "analysis_notes": [
    "Failure class is re-derived from the message at analysis time, not read from the record, because the run spans a change to the rule (METHODS 10.9). Resume re-derives it too, so the two agree.",
    "The trend test in 8.5.1 was not pre-registered and is exploratory (METHODS 10.10). The K = 30 rung was added after the first pass (METHODS 10.11).",
    "The factor-against-linear likelihood ratio in 8.5.1 is unclustered and is a shape diagnostic, not a standalone p-value. It cannot establish linearity; it failed to detect curvature (METHODS 8.5.1).",
    "Same-lane replacement is implemented and covers a replaced unit's whole ladder (METHODS 8.4). It had not run when these records were collected, so 120 planned calls were never completed; they sit in the middle rungs, and seven of 464 endpoint clusters were lost to the pairing requirement (METHODS 10.12).",
    "`packing reproduce` covers METHODS 8.1, 8.3, 8.3.2 and 8.5. The calibration gate needs `packing calibration-report`; the ladder diagnostics in 8.5.2 and 8.5.3 need `packing ladder-analyze`. Use `--strict` to fail on any computed value that is not pinned."
  ],
